# Registry conventions

## Folder shape

One folder per component: `registry/components/<slug>/`, slug kebab-case and
equal to `meta.ts`'s `slug`.

- `component.tsx` — required entry point; the build walks its imports.
- `demo.tsx` — required; `export default` a component, import from `./component`.
- `meta.ts` — required metadata.
- Anything else colocated (`use-x.ts`, `*.module.css`, `demo-<variant>.tsx`) is
  imported with `"./…"` and picked up automatically.

## Imports

- `cn` is at `@/lib/utils`. Never re-path it, copy it or redeclare it.
- Shared hooks → `hooks/use-x.ts` (`@/hooks/use-x`).
- Shared non-hook helpers → `lib/x.ts` (`@/lib/x`).
- shadcn primitives → `@/components/ui/<name>`.
- Single-use helpers stay in the component's own folder.
- Never import app-level code (`@/components/*` outside `components/ui/`,
  `@/data/*`): consumers don't have it.

## Metadata

`meta.ts` calling `defineComponent` is the only place metadata lives — no
separate categories, credits or meta JSON files anywhere.

- Contract: `registry/schema.ts`. It validates at module load, so bad metadata
  fails the build.
- `categories` must come from the closed `CATEGORIES` list in that file.
- `inspiration` is mandatory for anything ported from another library:
  `source`, `url`, `relationship` (`port` | `adaptation` | `inspired-by` |
  `original`). Designers depend on this attribution.
- `dependencies` / `registryDependencies` are declarations; the build also
  infers them from real imports.

## Generated — never hand-edit

`registry.json`, `public/r/`, `public/docs/`, `public/llms.txt`,
`registry/__generated__/`. Change `meta.ts` or the component and rebuild.

## Commands

- `npm run registry:intake -- <url-or-file>` — import from another library.
- `npm run registry:enrich` — fill props and behaviour tags from source; only
  writes empty fields, safe to re-run.
- `npm run registry:build` — regenerate all artifacts.
- `npm run registry:attribute` — fill inspiration from URLs in source comments.

## Porting a component

Use `scripts/v2/intake.mts` (via `registry:intake`) instead of copying files by
hand: it normalises `cn` and the source library's aliases, promotes hooks/lib
files without overwriting ours, and pre-fills attribution. Then fill in the
metadata it lists as TODO.

## Done means

A demo that isn't an intake scaffold, at least one real category
(`"Uncategorized"` is triage, not an answer), and a `description`. Until then
`status` stays `"needs-review"` — or `"draft"` while the demo is a scaffold.

## Style

Tabs, double quotes, semicolons. Comments explain *why*, never restate the code.
